  "visual_findings": {
    "close": "Exposed ground to the right of the pale strip has substantially fewer brown clouds, black pit chains and gouge-like marks. It now reads as a restrained light dry mineral surface with fine grain. Close detail is modest rather than the strongly resolved pebble detail of the Shujaiya close view.",
    "middle": "Cloudy dark mottling around the plaza and building lots is reduced. The ground is more coherent and restrained but averages to a very pale, fairly uniform surface. Contact and layer contrast remain weak in places.",
    "wide": "Source replacement retains the existing city layout and a coherent dry palette. Large bare areas remain visually uniform, with faint directional repeat and broad angular shading still visible.",
    "existing_boundary": "The pale smooth strip outlines, isolated dark sliver marks, road patches and sharp surface transitions remain visible. Their contrast against the replaced ground changes; this review does not claim the material edit repairs their geometry or proves their cause."
  },
  "remaining_limitations": [
    "The material result remains broadly pale and uniform at middle and wide distances; it does not establish the quality of the selected reference demonstrations.",
